{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "ASV1901",
  "book_code": "JOB",
  "chapter": 14,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Man, that is born of a woman,\nIs of few days, and full of trouble.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "He cometh forth like a flower, and is cut down:\nHe fleeth also as a shadow, and continueth not.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And dost thou open thine eyes upon such a one,\nAnd bringest me into judgment with thee?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Who can bring a clean thing out of an unclean? not one.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Seeing his days are determined,\nThe number of his months is with thee,\nAnd thou hast appointed his bounds that he cannot pass;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Look away from him, that he may rest,\nTill he shall accomplish, as a hireling, his day.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "For there is hope of a tree,\nIf it be cut down, that it will sprout again,\nAnd that the tender branch thereof will not cease.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though the root thereof wax old in the earth,\nAnd the stock thereof die in the ground;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet through the scent of water it will bud,\nAnd put forth boughs like a plant.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But man dieth, and is laid low:\nYea, man giveth up the ghost, and where is he?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "As",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the waters fail from the sea,\nAnd the river wasteth and drieth up;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So man lieth down and riseth not:\nTill the heavens be no more, they shall not awake,\nNor be roused out of their sleep.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Oh that thou wouldest hide me in Sheol,\nThat thou wouldest keep me secret, until thy wrath be past,\nThat thou wouldest appoint me a set time, and remember me!",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "If a man die, shall he live ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "again",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": "?\nAll the days of my warfare would I wait,\nTill my release should come.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou wouldest call, and I would answer thee:\nThou wouldest have a desire to the work of thy hands.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But now thou numberest my steps:\nDost thou not watch over my sin?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "My transgression is sealed up in a bag,\nAnd thou fastenest up mine iniquity.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But the mountain falling cometh to nought;\nAnd the rock is removed out of its place;",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The waters wear the stones;\nThe overflowings thereof wash away the dust of the earth:\nSo thou destroyest the hope of man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Thou prevailest for ever against him, and he passeth;\nThou changest his countenance, and sendest him away.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "His sons come to honor, and he knoweth it not;\nAnd they are brought low, but he perceiveth it not of them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "JOB.14.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "ASV1901:JOB.14.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "But his flesh upon him hath pain,\nAnd his soul within him mourneth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    }
  ]
}
